.TH NGINX-MON 1 "July 2026" "nginx-mon 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nginx-mon \- real-time Nginx reverse-proxy traffic monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nginx-mon
.RI [ --log-file " PATH" ]
.RI [ --detect-nginx ]
.RI [ --nginx-pid " PID" ]
.RI [ --enable-global-json-log ]
.RI [ --disable-global-json-log ]
.RI [ --toggle-global-json-log ]
.RI [ --global-log-path " PATH" ]
.RI [ --refresh-interval " SECONDS" ]
.RI [ --max-records " COUNT" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nginx-mon
tails an Nginx JSON access log and displays upstream traffic grouped by
frontend virtual host. It retains a bounded in-memory request history. By
default it locates one active nginx-mon JSON log through the running Nginx
process descriptors under
.IR /proc .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --log-file PATH
Explicit nginx-mon JSON access log to follow. This bypasses autodetection.
.TP
.B --detect-nginx
Explicitly request automatic discovery, which is already the default. It
locates one running Nginx master and follows its only open, nonempty access log
that matches nginx-mon's JSON log format. This Linux-only behavior reads
.IR /proc ;
it does not execute Nginx or parse its configuration. If discovery is
ambiguous or no matching log has traffic yet, use
.BR --log-file .
.TP
.B --nginx-pid PID
Locate the monitor log for the specified running Nginx master process. This
also enables discovery. An explicit
.B --log-file
takes precedence over both discovery options.
.TP
.B --enable-global-json-log
Add an nginx-mon managed include to the running Nginx instance's main
configuration file, inside its top-level
.B http
block. The fragment defines a JSON log format and adds an additional global
default access log. Existing global logs remain unchanged. The command runs
.B nginx -t
and sends HUP to the selected master only after validation succeeds. It
requires permission to modify the Nginx configuration and signal the process.
For process-control safety, nginx-mon manages only a master owned by the same
effective user.
.TP
.B --disable-global-json-log
Remove only the marked include and fragment created by
.BR --enable-global-json-log ,
then validate and reload the selected Nginx master.
.TP
.B --toggle-global-json-log
Enable the nginx-mon managed global log when it is absent, or disable it when
it is present. The operation recognizes only nginx-mon's marked include and
fragment. Use explicit enable or disable commands in automation where the
desired target state must be fixed.
.TP
.B --global-log-path PATH
JSON log path used by
.B --enable-global-json-log
or when the toggle enables the log.
The default is
.IR /var/log/nginx/nginx-mon-access.json.log .
The parent directory must exist and be writable by the Nginx master.
.TP
.B --refresh-interval SECONDS
Positive table refresh interval. The default is 1 second.
.TP
.B --max-records COUNT
Positive number of recent requests retained for the detail view. The default
is 5000.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up/Down
Move through frontend rows or detail rows.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the requests for the highlighted frontend.
.TP
.B Escape
Return from request detail to the live frontend table.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the log and table immediately.
.TP
.B p
Pause or resume live log ingestion and table updates. The displayed traffic is
frozen while paused.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl-C
Quit the monitor.
.SH NGINX LOG FORMAT
Install the supplied
.IR nginx_mon.conf
under Nginx's included configuration directory. It writes JSON records using
the upstream byte variables. Backend TX is
.BR $upstream_bytes_sent ,
the bytes Nginx sent to the upstream. Backend RX is
.BR $upstream_bytes_received ,
the bytes Nginx received from the upstream. A request with multiple upstream
attempts can contain comma-separated values; nginx-mon sums them.
.PP
The detail view also displays the TCP source endpoint from
.BR $remote_addr : $remote_port ,
the Nginx listener port from
.BR $server_port ,
and TLS protocol from
.BR $ssl_protocol .
.PP
The monitor uses the listener address from
.BR $server_addr
with NetworkManager to display the active network connection name, for example
.IR ens18 .
If NetworkManager does not own the interface, the interface name is used;
unavailable network information is shown as a dash.
An empty SSL protocol is displayed as Plain. When Nginx is behind another
proxy, configure its real IP module to log the original client address.
.PP
For a source-built Nginx, put the supplied log format in the existing
.B http
configuration and its access log directive in the deployed proxy server. The
sample test server and its RPM paths are not required. The account running
.B nginx-mon
must be able to read the access log and the selected process descriptors under
.IR /proc .
An ordinary combined-format access log cannot supply nginx-mon's upstream,
listener, and TLS fields; configure the supplied JSON log format and generate
at least one request before automatic discovery.
.PP
The managed global log is inherited only by virtual hosts without their own
.B access_log
directive. Add the JSON log explicitly to any virtual host that defines one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/nginx-mon/nginx_mon.conf
Sample Nginx log format and reverse-proxy server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8)
